---
import BaseLayout from '../../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout lang="en" title="[Free Event | Zoom] Agentic Guandan (掼蛋) · Opening Workshop" description="Join us this Saturday noon for an 1-hour workshop on AI Agents & Guandan strategies, warming up for the 3rd NCCAF Guandan Tournament on August 29." path="/en/posts/2026-08-21-agentic-guandan-opening-class/">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-12 md:py-20">
    <a href="/en/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 text-sm text-blue-500 hover:text-blue-400 mb-8 transition-colors">
      <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i>
      <span>Back to Home</span>
    </a>

    <article class="space-y-8">
      <header class="border-b border-slate-900 pb-8 space-y-4">
        <div class="flex items-center gap-x-3 text-xs text-slate-500 mb-2">
          <time datetime="2026-08-21">August 21, 2026</time>
          <span>·</span>
          <span class="px-2.5 py-0.5 rounded-full bg-blue-600/10 text-blue-400 border border-blue-500/20 font-semibold">Event Notice</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white leading-tight">
          🎴 [Free Event | Zoom] Agentic Guandan (掼蛋) · Opening Workshop
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 flex items-center gap-x-2">
          <span>Organizers: ZJUAANC, NACUAA</span>
        </p>
      </header>

      <div class="text-slate-300 space-y-6 leading-relaxed text-base">
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-200 font-medium">
          Hello alumni and friends!
        </p>
        <p>
          This Saturday noon, NACUAA NorCal Chapter and ZJUAANC jointly present the <strong>"Agentic Guandan (掼蛋) · Opening Workshop"</strong>.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 bg-slate-900/80 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-2xl text-slate-300 text-sm italic leading-relaxed">
          Combining classical card strategy with AI agent techniques. An 1-hour breakdown of game scenarios and card logic, followed by practice sessions warming up for the upcoming tournament!
        </div>

        <!-- Video Replay Callout Box -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-950/80 via-slate-900/90 to-purple-950/80 border-2 border-blue-500/50 rounded-3xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-5 shadow-2xl">
          <div class="space-y-1">
            <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-red-600/20 text-red-400 border border-red-500/30 text-xs font-bold">
              <i class="fa-solid fa-circle-play animate-pulse"></i>
              <span>Full Video Recording Available</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mt-1">🎬 [Video Replay] Agentic Guandan (掼蛋) · Opening Workshop</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">The workshop has concluded successfully. Click the button to watch the complete HD replay on YouTube.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="https://youtu.be/3-X-DXRQL64" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-6 py-3.5 bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-500 text-white font-bold text-sm rounded-2xl shrink-0 transition-colors shadow-lg flex items-center gap-x-2">
            <i class="fa-brands fa-youtube text-base"></i>
            <span>Watch Full Replay</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- RSVP Callout Box -->
        <div class="p-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-blue-950/60 to-purple-950/60 border border-blue-800/40 rounded-3xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-4 shadow-xl">
          <div>
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white mb-1">🎟️ Free Event Registration</h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300">RSVP on Luma to receive future event updates and reminders.</p>
          </div>
          <a href="https://luma.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-500 text-white font-semibold text-sm rounded-2xl shrink-0 transition-colors shadow-lg flex items-center gap-x-2">
            <span>RSVP on Luma</span>
            <i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-up-right-from-square text-xs"></i>
          </a>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">🏆 Target Event</h3>
        <div class="p-5 bg-slate-900/60 border border-slate-800 rounded-2xl space-y-2">
          <p class="font-bold text-white text-base">3rd NCCAF (华体会) Guandan Tournament · 4-Player Teams</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-300">
            <li><strong>Date & Time</strong>: Saturday, Aug 29, 1:30 PM PDT onwards (Cont'd Aug 30)</li>
            <li><strong>Location</strong>: 1591 McCarthy Blvd, Milpitas, CA 95035 (California Science and Technology University)</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">🎯 Who Should Attend</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Complete Beginners</strong> — Learn rules, card logic, and fundamental team strategies from scratch.</li>
          <li><strong>Experienced Players</strong> — Explore scenario analysis and how AI agents assist card tracking, replay, and practice (without replacing player judgment).</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">📅 Date & Time</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
          <li><strong>Pacific Time (PDT)</strong>: Saturday, Aug 22, 1:00 PM – 2:00 PM</li>
          <li><strong>Eastern Time (EDT)</strong>: Saturday, Aug 22, 4:00 PM – 5:00 PM</li>
          <li><strong>Beijing Time (CST)</strong>: Sunday, Aug 23, 4:00 AM – 5:00 AM</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">🎥 Format</h3>
        <p>
          <strong>Zoom Online</strong>, ~60 minutes; follow-up practice match. <strong>Free and public</strong>.<br />
          <strong>RSVP Link</strong>: <a href="https://luma.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-blue-400 hover:underline font-semibold">https://luma.com/</a><br />
          <span class="text-slate-400 text-sm">(Zoom link sent to WeChat groups & registered Luma emails prior to start)</span>
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">📋 Outline</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Guandan Rules & Teamwork Basics</strong> (Beginner-friendly)</li>
          <li><strong>Scenario Breakdown & Strategic Principles</strong></li>
          <li><strong>How AI Agents Assist</strong> (Tracking, Replay, Practice), Boundaries & Best Practices</li>
          <li><strong>Post-Workshop Practice Info & Aug 29 Tournament Warmup Tips</strong></li>
          <li><strong>Interactive Q&A</strong></li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">🎙️ Guest Speakers & Lecturers</h3>
        <div class="p-6 bg-slate-900/80 border border-slate-800 rounded-3xl space-y-6">
          <!-- Michael HUO (霍明旭) -->
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-start">
            <img src="/images/michael.jpg" alt="Michael HUO (霍明旭)" class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-blue-500 shrink-0 shadow-lg" />
            <div class="space-y-2 flex-1">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Michael HUO (霍明旭)</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                Former Zhejiang University faculty with 28 years of software & systems experience; Founding Board Member & Vice President of ZJUAANC; President of NACUAA AI Entrepreneurship Club; Chairman of VI AI Foundation.
              </p>
              <div class="p-3 bg-blue-950/40 border-l-4 border-blue-500 rounded-r-xl text-xs text-blue-300 font-medium">
                <strong>Opening Keynote (10-15 mins)</strong>: How beginners can leverage AI agents to accelerate learning from scratch to mastery.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <hr class="border-slate-800" />

          <!-- Tracy LI (李泉) -->
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-start">
            <img src="/images/tracy.jpg" alt="Tracy LI (李泉)" class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-purple-500 shrink-0 shadow-lg" />
            <div class="space-y-2 flex-1">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">Tracy LI (李泉)</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                B.S. in EE from Southeast University; Ph.D. in Economics from Washington State University; 2026 AI Scholar; 20+ years of risk management experience at US Fortune 500 financial institutions; Former Senior Director; Longtime on-duty volunteer at New Hope Chinese Cancer Care Foundation; Leadership of Suzhou High School Silicon Valley Alumni Association.
              </p>
              <div class="p-3 bg-purple-950/40 border-l-4 border-purple-500 rounded-r-xl text-xs text-purple-300 font-medium">
                <strong>Featured Session (20 mins)</strong>: How to utilize the AI Guandan Coach to rapidly elevate gameplay, foster community friendships, and promote cultural exchange from Silicon Valley to the world.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <hr class="border-slate-800" />

          <!-- James JIANG (蒋建良) -->
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 items-start">
            <img src="/images/jiang.jpg" alt="James JIANG (蒋建良)" class="w-20 h-20 rounded-full object-cover border-2 border-amber-500 shrink-0 shadow-lg" />
            <div class="space-y-2 flex-1">
              <h4 class="text-lg font-bold text-white">James JIANG (蒋建良)</h4>
              <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
                Shanghai Jiao Tong University alumnus, former President of SJTU Alumni Association of Southern California, Honorary President of NACUAA Guandan Club. Led the SJTU Alumni Team 1 to win the championship at the <a href="https://icitynews.com/?p=457002" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-amber-400 hover:underline">4th NACUAA Duplicate Guandan Tournament</a> (taking home the team trophy, medals, and $2,000 grand prize).
              </p>
              <div class="p-3 bg-amber-950/40 border-l-4 border-amber-500 rounded-r-xl text-xs text-amber-300 font-medium">
                <strong>Special Guest Keynote</strong>: Sharing tournament championship secrets, duplicate format winning strategies, board control, and live competitive mindset.
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">📱 WeChat Group & Contact</h3>
        <p>
          Add WeChat ID <strong><code>zjuaanc</code></strong> with note "Guandan Workshop" to join the WeChat discussion group.
        </p>
        <div class="my-6 text-center">
          <a href="/images/zjuaanc_wechat_qr.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-block group">
            <img src="/images/zjuaanc_wechat_qr.jpg" alt="WeChat ID zjuaanc" class="w-64 h-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-800 shadow-xl mx-auto group-hover:border-blue-500/50 transition-colors" />
          </a>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-400 mt-2">Scan QR Code to add WeChat ID (zjuaanc) to join the group</p>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white border-l-4 border-blue-500 pl-3">🏛️ Organizers & Partners</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-1 text-sm text-slate-300">
          <li><strong>Organizers</strong>: ZJUAANC, NACUAA</li>
          <li><strong>Co-Organizers</strong>: AI Agent Alliance, ZJU AI Agents, ViaAI Foundation, ViaAI Public Welfare Foundation</li>
          <li><strong>Supporting Partners</strong>: Tennessee, Philadelphia, Rhode Island, Florida ZJU Alumni Associations; NACUAA NorCal, Silicon Valley, Washington State, Washington DC, North Carolina, South Carolina Chapters; NACUAA AI Venture Club</li>
          <li><strong>Media Partner</strong>: North Alpha Post (北美发布)</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="text-sm text-slate-300 pt-4">
          This event is free and public.<br />
          Feel free to share with interested alumni and card lovers!
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
